From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:15:26 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/79] compute lane: a per-family binding names the knobs and
 the built-in tool

core/compute_binding.zig: a Binding is a knob prefix (TF_COMPUTE_LANE by
default), an optional family alias, and the Tool the server offers (name,
opt-in type, the compute default's min max_tokens). A boot sets the generic
names or the alias, not both (BadKnob).

- dsv41: generic names or TF_DSV41_COMPUTE_LANE* as before; the tool is
  python / code_interpreter / 1024, so its definition bytes are unchanged.
- flashnext: generic names only; a stub its serve engine does not read yet.

The server reads Info.compute_tool for the tool's name, opt-in type and
min_tokens; the existing one-argument helpers keep the default binding.
